{title: Oh! Susanna}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
I [C]come from Ala[F]bama with my [G7]banjo on my [C]knee,
I'm [C]going to Loui[F]siana, my [G7]true love for to [C]see.

{c: Chorus}
Oh! Su[F]sanna, [C]don't you cry for [G7]me,
For I [C]come from Ala[F]bama with my [G7]banjo on my [C]knee.

{c: Verse 2}
It [C]rained all night the [F]day I left, the [G7]weather it was [C]dry,
The [C]sun so hot I [F]froze to death, Su[G7]sanna, don't you [C]cry.
